.TH FKTRIM 3 2026-09-24 "fkstring" "fkstring Library Manual"
.nh
.SH NAME
fkltrim, fkrtrim, fktrim \- strip whitespace from the ends of an fkstring
.SH LIBRARY
fkstring library
.RI ( libfkstring ,\~ \-lfkstring )
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <fkstring.h>
.PP
.BI "size_t fkltrim(fkstring *" fks );
.BI "size_t fkrtrim(fkstring *" fks );
.BI "size_t fktrim(fkstring *" fks );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR fkltrim ()
removes whitespace from the start of
.IR fks ,
.BR fkrtrim ()
from its end, and
.BR fktrim ()
from both ends, in place.
.PP
Whitespace means the six bytes of the regular-expression
.B \es
class: space,
.BR \(aq\et\(aq ,
.BR \(aq\en\(aq ,
.BR \(aq\er\(aq ,
.BR \(aq\ef\(aq ,
and
.BR \(aq\ev\(aq .
Unlike
.BR isspace (3),
this does not depend on the locale.
.PP
The buffer is then shrunk by the same rule as
.BR fkstrtrunc (3).
A string that is all whitespace becomes empty.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The new length of
.IR fks ,
or 0 if
.I fks
is NULL.
.SH ERRORS
These functions do not return on allocation failure; see
.BR fkstring (3).
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
fkstring *s = fkstrnew("\et hello world \en");
\&
fktrim(s);    /* returns 11; s is "hello world" */
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fkstring (3),
.BR fkremove (3),
.BR fkstrtrunc (3)
